<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept">

  <name>Introduction</name>
  <type>concept:Introduction</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A short introduction to MachineBlocks</is>

  <documentation>
    MachineBlocks is a parametric system for generating LEGO-compatible 3D blocks. Primary use is
    3D printing (STL / 3MF); the same geometry model also supports general 3D modeling workflows.

    The system is a foundation for modular, printable machines: bricks, panels, enclosures, and
    functional assemblies built from typed, parameterized blocks.

    MachineBlocks is a domain on top of BlockML. Authoring uses MBML (MachineBlocks Markup
    Language). The canonical representation is MBOM (MachineBlocks Object Model). Render targets —
    OpenSCAD is the reference — serialize MBOM into target-specific output. Direct OpenSCAD Block
    Files remain supported as an advanced and legacy authoring path.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:Architecture" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — layered architecture MBML → MBOM → render target.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/03_mbom.md" relation="DeepDive">
      MBOM domain model — BlockML MD companion.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/00_system.md" relation="DeepDive">
      BlockML system overview — packages and conventions.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
